s in either denominator that we can exploit.\n\nTo do this, we multiply the top and bottom of the first fraction by $3$, and the top and bottom of the second fraction by $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{x(1+z)}+\\frac{1}{3(1+z)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{3}\\cdot \\frac{2}{x(1+z)}+\\frac{x}{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3(1+z)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6}{3x(1+z)}+\\frac{x}{3x(1+z)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6+x}{3x(1+z)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f" "basis" 319 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd97fb72cc78cc05c3db63fb0e5f5cc9787dc127dcf8f8322efb3a286f7b38a" "basis" 319 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f" "basis" 319 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6x(1+z)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a76765