\\\\ \\frac{2w-3+2wz-2w}{(z-1)(2w-3)} & = \\\\ \\frac{2wz-3}{(z-1)(2w-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f"} {"question" "q-70295" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd97fb72cc78cc05c3db63fb0e5f5cc9787dc127dcf8f8322efb3a286f7b38a"} {"question" "q-70295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f"} {"question" "q-70295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2wz-3z}{(z-1)(2w-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2wz-3}{(z-1)(2w-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2wz-4w-3}{(z-1)(2w-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2wz-4z+3}{(z-1)(2w-3)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4w-2wz}{(z-1)(2w-3)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f"} {"question" "q-70295" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2wz-3}{(z-1)(2w-3)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f"} {"question" "q-113217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write $3+\\frac{5-p}{p}$ as a single fraction." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f"} {"question" "q-113217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the fact that $3=\\frac{3}{1},$ we can write the expression as\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{5-p}{p}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. So, we put both fractions over a common denominator of $p$ by multiplying the top and bottom of the first fraction by $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{p}{p}\\cdot \\frac{3}{1}+\\frac{5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{3p}{p}+\\frac{5-p}{p}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the fractions and simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3p}{p}+\\frac{5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{3p+5-p}{p} & = \\\\ \\frac{2p+5}{p}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f"} {"question" "q-113217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd97fb72cc78cc05c3db63fb0e5f5cc9787dc127dcf8f8322efb3a286f7b38a"} {"question" "q-113217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930176/state.json" "file_sha256" "25a8d74ef2f25f2e11cad5ff5b3c8cd2302c2a767650593a9cd27f03d529066f"} {"question" "q-113217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2(p+5)}{p}"] ["math" "\\frac{2p+5}{p}"] ["math" "\\frac{2p-5}{p}"] ["math" "\\frac{p+5}{p}"] ["math" "\\frac{p-5}{p}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/